  "wrapper_source": "typedef unsigned int u32;\ntypedef unsigned long long u64;\n\nstruct iovec { const char *data; u32 length; };\n__attribute__((import_module(\"fib\"), import_name(\"fibonacci\")))\nextern int fibonacci(int);\n__attribute__((import_module(\"wasi_snapshot_preview1\"), import_name(\"clock_time_get\")))\nextern u32 clock_time_get(u32 clock, u64 precision, u64 *time);\n__attribute__((import_module(\"wasi_snapshot_preview1\"), import_name(\"fd_write\")))\nextern u32 fd_write(u32 fd, const struct iovec *buffers, u32 count, u32 *written);\n\nstatic void print(const char *data, u32 length) {\n  struct iovec buffer = {data, length};\n  u32 written;\n  if (fd_write(1, &buffer, 1, &written) || written != length) __builtin_trap();\n}\n\nstatic void number(u64 value, u32 width) {\n  char digits[32];\n  u32 offset = sizeof(digits);\n  do { digits[--offset] = '0' + value % 10; value /= 10; }\n  while (value || sizeof(digits) - offset < width);\n  print(digits + offset, sizeof(digits) - offset);\n}\n\nstatic u64 now(void) {\n  u64 time;\n  if (clock_time_get(1, 1, &time)) __builtin_trap();\n  return time;\n}\n\n__attribute__((export_name(\"main\")))\nvoid benchmark(void) {\n  const int expected[] = {17711, 28657, 46368, 75025};\n  for (int n = 22; n <= 25; n++)\n    if (fibonacci(n) != expected[n - 22]) __builtin_trap();\n  u64 checksum = 0, started = now();\n  for (int repeat = 0; repeat < 64; repeat++)\n    for (int n = 22; n <= 25; n++)\n      checksum += (u64)(n + 1) * (u32)fibonacci(n);\n  u64 elapsed = now() - started;\n  if (checksum != 269118144) __builtin_trap();\n  print(\"checksum: \", 10); number(checksum, 1);\n  print(\"\\nelapsed: \", 10); number(elapsed / 1000000000, 1);\n  print(\".\", 1); number(elapsed % 1000000000, 9); print(\" s\\n\", 3);\n}\n",
  "reproduction_notes": "# Throwaway Wastrel evaluation, 2026-10-10\n\nSource: https://codeberg.org/andywingo/wastrel.git\nPinned commit: ad0b577df0773a1fc825b2a2455e23bf03ea9dcc\nNo compiler source patches; all work is under /tmp.\n\n## Build\n\n```\ngit clone --depth 1 https://codeberg.org/andywingo/wastrel.git /tmp/snail-wastrel-20261010\ncd /tmp/snail-wastrel-20261010\nnix-shell -p guile autoconf automake pkg-config boehmgc --run './bootstrap.sh && ./configure && make -j4'\nmkdir -p build-tmp\nnix-shell -p guile pkg-config boehmgc --run 'TMPDIR=/tmp/snail-wastrel-20261010/build-tmp ./pre-inst-env bin/wastrel compile --gc=bdw --expose-dir=/ --preserve-builddir -o /tmp/snail-wastrel-20261010/cpu-bench /tmp/snail-wastrel-driver-20261010/benchmark.wasm'\n```\n\nThe normal filesystem sandbox fails with `unshare: Invalid argument` in this\nexecution environment. The documented `--expose-dir=/` option omits that\nnamespace setup. This benchmark only uses monotonic time and stdout.\n\nGuile 3.0.11, GCC 15.3.0, BDWGC 8.2.12. Default Wastrel optimized compilation\nuses -O2 and LTO. One module compilation took approximately 0.8 seconds,\nincluding nix-shell startup; this is a rough observation, not a timed build\ncomparison.\n\n## Inputs and outputs\n\nParent prepared `/tmp/snail-wastrel-driver-20261010/benchmark.wasm` by merging\na C-to-Wasm WASI benchmark wrapper with our existing WasmGC Fibonacci module.\nOnly the original module's unused linear-memory declaration/export was removed\nto retain one memory. Computational functions were unchanged. Wrapper source\nand intermediate Wasm remain in the driver directory. It warms Fibonacci\n22..25, then measures 64 repetitions of weighted Fibonacci 22..25 with\nclock_time_get(CLOCK_MONOTONIC). Expected checksum: 269118144.\n\nBinaries:\n\n- `cpu-bench`: standard -O2 + LTO + Nix defaults.\n- `cpu-bench-o3`: -O3 + LTO + Nix defaults.\n- `cpu-bench-o2-nozero`: -O2 + LTO, only Nix zerocallusedregs removed.\n- `cpu-bench-o3-nozero`: -O3 + LTO, only Nix zerocallusedregs removed.\n\nAll execute successfully with checksum 269118144. Initial unpinned serial\nsamples: standard O2 0.070803395 s, O2-nozero 0.063693695 s, O3-nozero\n0.066245857 s. Parent performs the controlled pinned interleaved comparison;\nthese preliminary samples should not be used for final ratios.\n\n`rebuild-nozero.py` reproduces the two clean variants; run it inside the same\nNix shell. `rebuild-nozero.log` records the original/filtered hardening\nenvironment and full compile/link commands. Removing only a compile-stage\n-fzero-call-used-regs flag was insufficient because GCC LTO linking reenabled\nit. The final script removes the `zerocallusedregs` token for both stages.\nOther hardening options are untouched. `*.fib.asm` show standard return paths\nwith six register-clearing XORs and clean variants without that sequence.\nGenerated C/header remain in `build-tmp/wastrel-JXZlcl/`.\n\n## Actual GC smoke test\n\n`quads-small.wat` is Wastrel's own `examples/quads.wat`, changing only the\nstarting depth from 10 to 7. Compiled with the standard CLI and --gc=bdw,\n`WASTREL_PRINT_STATS=1 ./quads-small` validated a live 21,845-node tree after\n60 allocations of 5,461-node garbage trees. Exit 0, two major collections,\npeak live data 1.294 MB. `ldd` confirms linkage to libgc.so.1. This validates\nactual allocation and collection separately from the CPU benchmark, whose\nhot path does not allocate.\n",
